# Changesets

Add a changeset only when it is a **new** user-facing change that is not already covered by a pending file in `.changeset/`. `pnpm version-packages` later consumes these files to bump versions and prepend entries to `CHANGELOG.md` (app) and each package changelog. Do **not** hand-edit `CHANGELOG.md` or run `pnpm version-packages` as part of feature work.

## When

- Required: first user-facing feat / fix / enhance / improvement / security that is not already covered by a pending changeset
- Skip: formatting-only, Cursor rules, comments, tests with no product change
- Skip: follow-up bugfixes, polish, or tweaks on work that already has a pending changeset (the feature is not released yet; a second changelog line is noise)

Check `.changeset/` before writing a new file. If this session (or an unreleased branch) already added a changeset for the feature, do **not** add another one for a later bugfix on that same work. Only write a new changeset if the follow-up is a **separate** user-facing change that the existing file does not describe. If the existing summary is now wrong, edit that file instead of adding a second one.

## How

Write a new `.changeset/<adjective>-<noun>.md` (do not run interactive `pnpm changeset`). List every affected `packages/*` name and the semver bump.

Deploys follow these bumps: the website, Cloudflare workers and PocketBase only ship when the Version Packages PR raises their version. The website also deploys on a `ui` / `api` / `i18n` / `game-data` / `shared-assets` bump; `api-gateway`, `jobs-worker`, `smurf-worker` and `pocketbase` only on their own. A package left out of the changeset is not deployed.

| Bump | Use for |
|------|---------|
| `patch` | bugfixes, small enhancements |
| `minor` | new features |
| `major` | breaking changes |

```markdown
---
'@company-of-heroes/app': patch
---

feat; highlight smurf accounts next to player names
```

Multiple packages:

```markdown
---
'@company-of-heroes/app': minor
'@company-of-heroes/pocketbase': patch
---

feat; add player ELO ratings from match results
```

## Summary style

One line per change, lowercase after the prefix, matching existing changelog voice:

- `feat; …` — new capability
- `fix; …` — bugfix
- `enhance;` / `improvement; …` — improvement to existing behavior
- `security; …` — security fix

```markdown
# ❌ BAD — extra changeset for a bugfix on unreleased work, or changelog hand-edit
.changeset/player-labels.md          ← already covers the feature
.changeset/player-labels-color-fix.md ← do not add this

# ✅ GOOD — one pending changeset per unreleased change
feat; highlight smurf accounts next to player names
```

## Do not

- Ship a **new** user-facing change with no changeset when none exists yet
- Add a second changeset for a bugfix or polish pass on work that already has a pending one
- Edit `CHANGELOG.md` or `packages/*/CHANGELOG.md` by hand (duplicates on version)
- Bump versions in `package.json` / `tauri.conf.json` / `Cargo.toml` yourself
